  "passed": false,
  "stage": "review",
  "problems": [
   "grammar: 'Han ikke gøre andet end at klage hele dagen' is ungrammatical Danish. The finite verb must be in the second position (V2 rule) and conjugated for tense. A correct version would be 'Han gør ikke andet end at klage hele dagen' (present) or 'Han gjorde ikke andet end at klage hele dagen' (past).",
   "translations: The English translation 'He did nothing but complain all day' uses past tense, but the Danish sentence uses present tense (though incorrectly formed). The Russian and Ukrainian translations also use past tense ('жаловался', 'скаржився'), which does not match the intended present tense of the Danish.",
   "The Danish sentence 'Han ikke gøre andet end at klage hele dagen.' is grammatically incorrect. It is missing the finite verb 'gør' and should be 'Han gør ikke andet end at klage hele dagen.'",
   "The English translation 'He did nothing but complain all day.' uses the past tense, while the Danish sentence attempts to use the present tense."
  ]
 },
